#!/bin/sh
# minmux CLI (macOS): hands its arguments to the minmux app — `minmux open …`, `minmux --help`.
# A running minmux takes the request and this returns at once; with none running, the app
# starts here (detached) and opens the pane once its workspace is restored.
# MINMUX_APP: the app to use (its .app bundle or its executable), else /Applications.
app=${MINMUX_APP:-}
if [ -z "$app" ]; then
  for c in /Applications/minmux.app "$HOME/Applications/minmux.app"; do
    if [ -d "$c" ]; then app=$c; break; fi
  done
fi
case $app in *.app | *.app/) app=${app%/}/Contents/MacOS/minmux ;; esac
if [ ! -x "$app" ]; then
  echo "minmux: app not found${app:+ at $app} (set MINMUX_APP to minmux.app)" >&2
  exit 127
fi

# A second instance exits within a second (usage / errors on its own stdout / stderr); the
# first one IS the app, so it must outlive this shell: in a session of its own (setsid via perl,
# which macOS ships; else nohup alone) — the caller's process group can end, or be killed (a
# sandboxed or scripted shell), without taking the app along — with its output in files that are
# relayed if it exits (else they stay, as its log, in $TMPDIR/minmux-cli.*).
#   - $MINMUX_CLI_READY appears: it holds the lock, it's the app → 0, left running.
#   - it exits: a second instance. An `open` wrote "pending" in $MINMUX_CLI_ACK before handing
#     its request over, and the app answers there ("ok", or why not): anything but "ok" is an
#     error, never a silent 0.
#   - neither within MINMUX_CLI_TIMEOUT seconds (12): the running app doesn't answer, and
#     Chromium would soon kill it (20s after this launch began) and start over in its place,
#     losing its panes. So this launch is killed instead, and it's an error (and the app drops
#     the request if it gets to it later: cli.ts STALE_MS).
dir=$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/minmux-cli.XXXXXX") || exit 1
detach=
if command -v perl >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  detach='perl -MPOSIX -e POSIX::setsid();exec(@ARGV)||die("minmux:$!\n")'
fi
# shellcheck disable=SC2086 # $detach is a command line on purpose
MINMUX_CLI_READY=$dir/ready MINMUX_CLI_ACK=$dir/ack nohup $detach "$app" "$@" \
  >"$dir/out" 2>"$dir/err" </dev/null &
pid=$!
deadline=$(($(date +%s) + ${MINMUX_CLI_TIMEOUT:-12}))
while kill -0 "$pid" 2>/dev/null; do
  if [ -e "$dir/ready" ]; then # it's the app: leave it running
    rm -f "$dir/ready" "$dir/ack" # its output stays in $dir (visible, deletable once it quits)
    exit 0
  fi
  if [ "$(date +%s)" -ge "$deadline" ]; then
    kill -9 "$pid" 2>/dev/null
    echo "minmux: the running minmux didn't answer; nothing was opened (it was left running)" >&2
    rm -rf "$dir"
    exit 1
  fi
  sleep 0.05
done
wait "$pid"
code=$?
cat "$dir/out"
cat "$dir/err" >&2
if [ "$code" -eq 0 ] && [ -e "$dir/ack" ]; then
  answer=$(cat "$dir/ack")
  if [ "$answer" != ok ]; then
    [ "$answer" = pending ] && answer="it never answered"
    echo "minmux: the running minmux didn't take the request: $answer" >&2
    code=1
  fi
fi
rm -rf "$dir"
exit "$code"
